WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.116 --> 00:00:06.595
I'm Randy Dietrich, Facilities and Maintenance
Director at Kestrel Falls Community

2
00:00:06.595 --> 00:00:07.195
Hospital.

3
00:00:06.909 --> 00:00:08.719
My memo's in your files.

4
00:00:08.719 --> 00:00:10.517
Let me tell you why I wrote it.

5
00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:16.613
To help pay for the new EHR, my budget for next
year drops one point one million

6
00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:19.721
dollars, from fourteen million to
twelve point nine.

7
00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:22.172
To fit that, I'd put off some work.

8
00:00:22.172 --> 00:00:27.344
Most of it can wait: painting, parking
lot repairs, lobby furniture.

9
00:00:27.344 --> 00:00:28.887
Some of it can't.

10
00:00:28.887 --> 00:00:32.660
The yearly full-load test of our
emergency generators.

11
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:37.331
New batteries for the backup power units
in forty-one network closets.

12
00:00:37.331 --> 00:00:40.713
Twenty-nine of those batteries are
more than five years old.

13
00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:45.485
And better cooling for the main server room,
which ran hot twice last summer.

14
00:00:45.485 --> 00:00:48.440
Here's why that's your
problem, not just mine.

15
00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.998
Every computer, scanner, and wireless access
point in this hospital depends on

16
00:00:52.998 --> 00:00:54.780
those closets.

17
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.936
If the power or the cooling fails on go-live
weekend, the new system goes down,

18
00:00:59.936 --> 00:01:02.178
even if the software works perfectly.

19
00:01:02.178 --> 00:01:04.871
My crew also installs the new equipment.

20
00:01:04.871 --> 00:01:09.758
About one hundred eighty more wall-mounted
workstations and charging stations.

21
00:01:09.758 --> 00:01:12.776
Fewer dollars means fewer hands.

22
00:01:12.776 --> 00:01:14.268
And one more thing.

23
00:01:14.268 --> 00:01:18.894
I asked to stay off the core team in February
because I had no hours to give.

24
00:01:18.894 --> 00:01:21.999
That didn't mean leave
Facilities out of planning.

25
00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:25.816
I found out about the cut
from a spreadsheet.

26
00:01:25.816 --> 00:01:31.057
What I need: the generator test and the
batteries funded no matter what,

27
00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:34.142
my crew's install work in the
project schedule,

28
00:01:34.142 --> 00:01:36.880
and one named contact on the
transition team.

